{
  "annotator_prompt": [
    {
      "name": "highlight_frame",
      "description": "Initially null. On the first cycle containing visible white circular areas beneath cubes, store the earliest frame in that cycle clearly showing the highlighted set. Retain that label thereafter, including after the highlights disappear. The white square supporting the button is not a cube highlight. e.g. \"E17\"",
      "value_type": "keyframe"
    },
    {
      "name": "button_pressed",
      "description": "Initially false. Set true at the first cycle showing the closed fingertips down in contact with the button after the pressing descent; the observed TCP may stop around z=0.024 rather than reaching the commanded z=0.0075. Keep true thereafter. Do not set true merely because highlights appear. e.g. false",
      "value_type": "boolean"
    },
    {
      "name": "lifted_count",
      "description": "Initially zero. Count distinct highlighted cubes whose completed pickup lift has been observed: the cube is held off the table and the TCP has reached approximately z=0.15. Increment at the cycle observing that lift, not at the grasp or at the cycle commanding the lift. Returning a cube to the table does not decrement the count. Targets are processed in red, green, blue color order, omitting unhighlighted colors; within a color use increasing world x, then increasing world y. e.g. 0",
      "value_type": "count"
    }
  ],
  "policy_prompt_for_memory": [
    {
      "name": "highlight_frame",
      "description": "Write null when memory is empty and no cube highlight has appeared. If the carried value is null, inspect all motion frames and store the earliest frame clearly showing white circular areas beneath the highlighted cubes. Ignore the white square beneath the button. Once a label is stored, carry it unchanged even when the white areas disappear. e.g. \"E17\""
    },
    {
      "name": "button_pressed",
      "description": "Initialize false. Set true when this cycle shows the closed fingertips down in contact with the button following a pressing descent, including a contact-limited TCP height around z=0.024. Otherwise preserve the carried value. Highlights alone do not establish a press. e.g. false"
    },
    {
      "name": "lifted_count",
      "description": "Initialize zero. Recover the highlighted identities from highlight_frame and order them red, green, blue, omitting unhighlighted colors; break same-color ties by increasing world x, then y. Increment the carried count by one only when this cycle shows the next not-yet-counted target held off the table with TCP approximately z=0.15 after lifting. A low grasp is not a completed lift. A still-held previously counted target must not increment it again. Preserve the count through release and retreat. e.g. 0"
    }
  ],
  "policy_prompt_for_action": "Start with an open hand and approach the button. Interpret all positions in world coordinates using the supplied camera calibration; estimate button and cube locations from their geometry, not raw image left/right. Use the wrist view to refine alignment. Recover target identities from highlight_frame after their white areas disappear, matching by position as well as color; never select every cube of a highlighted color. Use the observations of this cycle together with carried memory to recognize newly completed presses and lifts before selecting the action.\n\nButton rules: If button_pressed is false and the hand is not yet above the button, move to its center at z=0.15, roll=-3.1416, pitch=0, yaw=0, gripper open. If above the button at approach height with open fingers, close at the same nominal approach waypoint. If above it with closed fingers and no observed contact yet, descend to its center at z=0.0075 with fingers closed. Once contact is observed, retract to the button center at z=0.15, keeping closed; do not repeat the press merely because the actual contact height is higher than the command. After retracting, open at the button approach waypoint before traveling to a cube.\n\nPickup rules: Order highlighted targets red, green, blue, with same-color ties by increasing world x then y. Select the first target not already represented by lifted_count. With open fingers and adequate table clearance, approach its center at z=0.15. Use roll=3.1416, pitch=0 and a yaw aligned to its horizontal square edges, choosing the equivalent square orientation in approximately [-0.7854,0.7854]. Once above that target, descend to its center at z=0.02 and close. Allow normal approach error of roughly 1–1.5 cm rather than repeatedly commanding the hover. With the cube grasped at low height, lift vertically to z=0.15 with fingers closed, preserving the aligned yaw. Estimate its grasp center from the visible cube and wrist geometry rather than treating a small TCP tracking error as a new target location.\n\nHandling additional targets: Once a pickup lift is visibly complete, it counts even if the cube is subsequently returned. If another highlighted target remains and a counted cube is still held at hover height, lower at the current TCP x,y to z=0.01, retaining current orientation, and open on arrival. If the hand is low and open over that returned cube, retract vertically to approximately z=0.15 with fingers open before moving laterally. When retracted, approach the next uncounted target, not the cube just returned. After lifting the final target, keep it held; success should end the episode without requiring a placement.\n\nEvery gripper-only change must include at least 2 mm of translation if its nominal waypoint would otherwise equal the reported TCP pose; use a small upward adjustment, within 5 mm. Do not advance memory on an action that executed no steps. If alignment or grasp evidence is ambiguous, use the current wrist image to correct the relevant object-centered approach at safe height; a failed empty grasp should be retried without counting it. If no target evidence has yet been captured after the button operation, use a short bounded wait specifically to observe the highlight display and inspect every returned frame. Do not invent targets or repeatedly press a confirmed button. For an otherwise unmatched situation, preserve known task facts, keep a visibly held cube closed, and retract vertically to safe clearance before reassessing."
}
